{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1063366-enter-the-squirrel","id":1063366,"title":"Enter the Squirrel","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-03-16T12:19:19-07:00","id":1063366,"title":"Enter the Squirrel","content":"So, based on another thread in the forums, someone suggested the creation of were-squirrels. I was wondering if anyone wanted to share their interpretation of the were-squirrel? My interpretation comes from the webcomic El Goonish Shive (though it is much less strong than Grace).<br /> <br /> I think that were-squirrels would have five forms (human, near human, hybrid, near squirrel, and squirrel) which would be comparable to the five Kitsune forms. The near human would have Dexterity+1, Stamina+1, and Manipulation-1. The hybrid form would be gain Dexterity+2, Stamina+2, Manipulation -1, and Perception+1. The near squirrel form would have Dexterity+3, Stamina+3, Manipulation-2, and Perception+1. The squirrel form would have Dexterity+4, Stamina+2, Manipulation-1, and Perception+2.<br /> <br /> In addition to their normal shapeshifting, were-squirrels would be able to learn additional forms during character creation for 3 freebie points each or after character creation for 3 XP. Each form would be a variation of one of their five basic forms and possess the strengths and weakness of the basic form that they are based on. What other features would you like a were-squirrel to have?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-16T12:23:33-07:00","id":1063368,"title":"","content":"I don't know that this warranted another thread entirely, but my proposed setup in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1061403-5th-edition-new-breeds?p=1063363#post1063363\">here </a>in the other thread.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1063366-enter-the-squirrel#post1063366\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I think that were-squirrels would have five forms (human, near human, hybrid, near squirrel, and squirrel) which would be comparable to the five Kitsune forms. The near human would have Dexterity+1, Stamina+1, and Manipulation-1. The hybrid form would be gain Dexterity+2, Stamina+2, Manipulation -1, and Perception+1. The near squirrel form would have Dexterity+3, Stamina+3, Manipulation-2, and Perception+1. The squirrel form would have Dexterity+4, Stamina+2, Manipulation-1, and Perception+2.</div> </div> </div> </div>If I were to do a full 5 form build, I would give the near human form +2 or 3 Dex and that's about it. -1 Man penalty.<br /> &quot;Crinos&quot; form: I think the Dex should be higher.<br /> Stamina in animal form seems way too high. I think the only reason the Ratkin (the closest equivalent) get +2 in Rodens is because they are supposed to be the embodiment of their patron Totem of survival.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1063366-enter-the-squirrel#post1063366\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> In addition to their normal shapeshifting, were-squirrels would be able to learn additional forms during character creation for 3 freebie points each or after character creation for 3 XP. Each form would be a variation of one of their five basic forms and possess the strengths and weakness of the basic form that they are based on. What other features would you like a were-squirrel to have?</div> </div> </div> </div>This is a kind of bizarre idea. No other shifter gets to add forms with freebies or XP (outside of learning specific form Gifts) so I would drop this entirely.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":805,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","user":"idpersona","date":". 03-16-2017, 03:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-16T12:32:35-07:00","id":1063377,"title":"","content":"I'm wondering, are there any famous legendary squirrels outside of the Norse Ratatoskr and the amazing Squirrel Girl?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-16T12:40:55-07:00","id":1063383,"title":"","content":"rocky the flying Squirel?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-16T12:45:15-07:00","id":1063389,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1063366-enter-the-squirrel?p=1063377#post1063377\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm wondering, are there any famous legendary squirrels outside of the Norse Ratatoskr and the amazing Squirrel Girl?</div> </div> </div> </div>A quick Google search shows a few Native American legends dealing with squirrels (<a href=\"http://www.native-languages.org/legends-squirrel.htm\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>).<br /> <br /> And if you're going to put Squirrel Girl in there, then I would include the squirrel from Ice age (the one that is always chasing the acorn).<br /> Edit: Wikipedia has a list of fictional squirrel characters <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_fictional_rodents_in_animation#Squirrels\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":805,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","user":"idpersona","date":". 03-16-2017, 03:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-16T16:09:46-07:00","id":1063615,"title":"","content":"Potential Hispo equivalent:<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://vignette3.wikia.nocookie.net/speculativeevolution/images/1/1b/Chiselhead.jpg/revision/latest?cb=20110811173655\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":758,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","user":"Ramnesis","date":".  Better quality picture. 03-17-2017, 07:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-17T02:24:49-07:00","id":1063781,"title":"","content":"Hmm, Dire Wolf, Megaladon, Saber Tooth Tigers for the <i>current</i> Hispo Forms....<br /> <br /> Aren't Saber Tooth Squirrels meant to look like <i>this?</i> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://imgcdn.geocaching.com/cache/dd9ceb6c-813a-42cf-b680-2ff325b07ffa.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4684-lin-liren","name":"Lin Liren","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-17T04:22:36-07:00","id":1063807,"title":"","content":"I would have scaled that one up to 7 feet and made it the Crinos. Then this would be the the Glabro:<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://homepage.univie.ac.at/horst.prillinger/blog/p/martincurry.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-17T07:36:29-07:00","id":1063844,"title":"","content":"hmmmn, would they have the same patagia gift the dancers have?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-17T08:54:13-07:00","id":1063888,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lin Liren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1063366-enter-the-squirrel?p=1063781#post1063781\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm, Dire Wolf, Megaladon, Saber Tooth Tigers for the <i>current</i> Hispo Forms....</div> </div> </div> </div>Respectively, too small to be Hispo, too large to be Chasmus, and about the same size as Chatro for the larger Bastet tribes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-17T13:01:50-07:00","id":1063987,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1063366-enter-the-squirrel?p=1063888#post1063888\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Respectively, too small to be Hispo, too large to be Chasmus, and about the same size as Chatro for the larger Bastet tribes.</div> </div> </div> </div>I kind of figured you'd chime in with those corrections. That (recurring, at least for Hispo/dire wolf) terminology really does seem to bother you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-17T13:15:20-07:00","id":1063999,"title":"","content":"The funny thing is, saber-tooth squirrels really did exist in the real life ice age, but we didn't know until fossils of them were discovered after the first Ice Age movie came out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-17T15:56:04-07:00","id":1064063,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1063366-enter-the-squirrel?p=1063987#post1063987\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I kind of figured you'd chime in with those corrections. That (recurring, at least for Hispo/dire wolf) terminology really does seem to bother you.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, dire wolves aren't shmeerps, so there is that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-17T18:16:02-07:00","id":1064104,"title":"","content":"I wanted to add my two cents on this since I kinda started this train.<br /> <br /> (<i><b>Warning</b></i> please excuse my grammar it's not the best.)<br /> <br /> <b><i>Sciuridae (Were-Squirrels)</i></b><br /> <br /> A few centuries ago Gaia gave birth to the Sciuridae and charged them with gathering spirits that have been bound into items and returning them to the umbra. Because of this duty, the Sciuridae maintain their life in the Preumbra where many talons and fetishes go missing or are forgotten. But since the turn of the century, they have noticed there are more items being lost and forgotten in the mortal world. The elders have started sending small groups out to find and return those bound spirits.<br /> <br /> <b>Breeding:</b> Sciuridae breed just like the Garou but Homid born are very rare since the most human contact they have is with those people who wonder into the preumbra by mistake and those who transverse it. It is not uncommon for Sciuridae to enter in the physical world to breed. Many of the kinfolks the Sciuridae have are Squirrels and Metis. <br /> <br /> <b>Natural abilities:</b> Sciuridae are immune to disconnection from staying in the Umbra for an extended timeframe. This life in the umbra allows them to speak and understand any spirit.<br /> <br /> <b>Natural flaws:</b> Due to their lean bodies and light weight they find it hard to resist damage as the other shifters +2 to all soak rolls. Also, a Sciuridae can be easily distracted when things take too long. All extended roles are at a +2 difficulty. Their command from Gaia is the only thing they seem to be able to focus on easily. Sciuridae follows Helios instead of Luna since the sun shines the light on those lost and forgotten. This means they suffer aggravated damage from gold instead of silver.<br /> <br /> <b>Black Squirrels</b> are a group of squirrels who turned their tails on their own people and Gaia. They seek to follow the Wyrm. Black squirrels no longer seek to free the lost and forgotten but to taint them and find them a home to taint. Black Squirrels have tainted rabies which prevents them from rolling to resist frenzy checks. This taint can be passed on even to other shifters and only a rite of cleansing can remove it. Like their name, Black Squirrels are solid black down to the bones and blood. In their homid hey have black eyes. It is said that the first of their kind tracked a fetish into the labyrinth but found it was just a trap and when it looked up it look into the wyrm and at that point, it turned it soul black.<br /> <br /> <b>Breed Forms:</b><br /> <br /> <b>Homid</b><br /> <br /> <i> No Change<br /> <br /> Difficulty: 6</i><br /> <br /> <b>Crinos:</b><br /> <br /> <i> Strength (+1)<br /> Dexterity (+4)<br /> Stamina (+2)<br /> Manipulation (-2)<br /> Appearance: -1<br /> <br /> Difficulty: 6<br /> <br /> Perception: +1<br /> <br /> INCITE DELIRIUM IN HUMANS</i><br /> <br /> <b>Squirrel:</b><br /> <br /> <i> Strength (+-1)<br /> Dexterity (+2)<br /> Stamina (+1)<br /> <br /> Difficulty: 6<br /> <br /> Perception: +3<br /> Dodge +3</i><br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Like the Sun I am relentless even in death...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3293-rahod","name":"Rahod","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-17T19:00:29-07:00","id":1064128,"title":"","content":"Ability bonuses to forms went out with 2nd edition (the Rokea got a pretty hefty bonus to Intimidation in 1e, but shed it by 2e).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-17T20:10:22-07:00","id":1064156,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3293-rahod\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3293\" data-vbnamecard=\"3293\">Rahod</a>, I like the writeup in general. I think the Crinos Stamina bonus is too high, but that's a minor nitpick (and <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar23_3.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"23\" data-vbnamecard=\"23\">Saur Ops Specialist</a> already mentioned the Dodge thing). The Natural Flaws section is a bit much. Corax and Hollow Boned Mokole don't even take a +2 penalty to soak. And +2 to all extended actions is also harsh.<br /> <br /> This sentence is also confusing: &quot;Many of the kinfolks the Sciuridae have are Squirrels and Metis.&quot; Metis aren't kinfolk since they're Fera. Maybe you meant that the Sciuridae are mostly squirrels and Metis?<br /> <br /> But all in all, I like the concept and stat spread. Good job.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-18T13:15:18-07:00","id":1064450,"title":"","content":"I see your point those points could be move or adjusted into something like Dexterity for a total of +3.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Like the Sun I am relentless even in death...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3293-rahod","name":"Rahod","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-18T13:19:36-07:00","id":1064456,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rahod</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1063366-enter-the-squirrel?p=1064450#post1064450\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I see your point those points could be move or adjusted into something like Dexterity for a total of +3.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would. <br /> <br /> And they could have access to a background similar to the Ratkin's Freak Factor background which could cover some common innate spirit tricks from their Umbral heritage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-18T13:23:46-07:00","id":1064458,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1063366-enter-the-squirrel?p=1064156#post1064156\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3293-rahod\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3293\" data-vbnamecard=\"3293\">Rahod</a>, I like the writeup in general. I think the Crinos Stamina bonus is too high, but that's a minor nitpick (and <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar23_3.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"23\" data-vbnamecard=\"23\">Saur Ops Specialist</a> already mentioned the Dodge thing). The Natural Flaws section is a bit much. Corax and Hollow Boned Mokole don't even take a +2 penalty to soak. And +2 to all extended actions is also harsh.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think both those natural difficulties could be lowered to +1 but I see they are needed to remain due to the frail nature of the squirrel and their short attention span. As for the dodge +3 any input would be helpful.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1063366-enter-the-squirrel?p=1064156#post1064156\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3293-rahod\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3293\" data-vbnamecard=\"3293\">Rahod</a>This sentence is also confusing: &quot;Many of the kinfolks the Sciuridae have are Squirrels and Metis.&quot; Metis aren't kinfolk since they're Fera. Maybe you meant that the Sciuridae are mostly squirrels and Metis?</div> </div> </div> </div>Let me correct my self here &quot;Most of the Sciuridae kinfolk are squirrels, due to the low population they welcome Metis as equals not as honored or shunned as other changers do.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Like the Sun I am relentless even in death...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3293-rahod","name":"Rahod","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-18T13:39:31-07:00","id":1064468,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rahod</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1063366-enter-the-squirrel?p=1064458#post1064458\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I think both those natural difficulties could be lowered to +1 but I see they are needed to remain due to the frail nature of the squirrel and their short attention span. As for the dodge +3 any input would be helpful.</div> </div> </div> </div>I might limit the +1 to soak to animal form then. Crinos should remind unaffected. The + to dodge can either be rolled in to a Dex bonus or an added dif to hit them (since they're small) or both.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Let me correct my self here &quot;Most of the Sciuridae kinfolk are squirrels, due to the low population they welcome Metis as equals not as honored or shunned as other changers do.&quot; </div> </div> </div>Ah okay. There is also precedent for Spirit heritage which would make sense for this Fera. You can also decide that either they don't have Metis at all or that their Metis don't suffer deformities (like Kitsune). In any of these cases, their Metis can be treated as equals.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-18T14:05:19-07:00","id":1064488,"title":"","content":"I agree with the +1 to soak in animal form and i would most likely put the bonus goes to dex to make it more simplified. I would say their metis don't suffer deformities like the Kitsune it makes more sense with their lower population and Gaia's need for this breed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Like the Sun I am relentless even in death...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3293-rahod","name":"Rahod","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-19T07:59:06-07:00","id":1064752,"title":"","content":"two things on squirells I'll mention here?<br /> <br /> 1: stats for them were curiously ommitted in chronicles of Darknesses animal stats things<br /> <br /> <br /> 2; a glasswalker theruge summoned up a squirel spirit was unsure on chiminage... pecan prailine sound good?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-ni